  

<h2 id="setapp-is-incredible-value-but-the-alternatives-are-pretty-good-too">Setapp is incredible value, but the alternatives are pretty good, too</h2>
<p><img src="https://cdn.blot.im/blog_177bc256f0ee469c998e912e20ece048/_image_cache/f920826c-ec8c-4019-af0b-8c2f71d56bff/pasted-percent20image-percent2020260914094704.png" alt="rough cartoon sketch of a stick figure holding a tiny sack walking away from a huge sack that has a $ price tag on it" width="1158" height="1130"></p>
<p>My Setapp subscription ran out last week; I am officially a former Setapp subscriber. After 6 years of happily paying one fee for access to more than 200 apps, it’s time for a break.</p>
<p>Not because I’m unhappy with the value (what you get is insanely good for the money), but because right now I need a little less in my life. Less choices, less distraction, less bills.</p>
<p>I still heartily recommend Setapp to Mac users who want a cost effective way to try out new apps, or who might need a way (<a href="https://ellanew.com/2020/08/26/i-was-a-task-management-app-addict" class="wikilink">as I did</a>) to short circuit their app addiction.</p>
<p>I’ve written before about the Setapp apps that work well with plain text. I’ve also explored preparing to leave Setapp, and researching alternatives to the apps I used most.</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://ellanew.com/2022/11/18/7-tools-make-setapp-worth-it" class="wikilink">2022-11-18 These Setapp Tools Alone Make the Subscription Worth It</a><br>
</li>
<li><a href="https://ellanew.com/2023/06/10/setapp-simplifies-a-plain-text-life" class="wikilink">2023-06-10 6 Setapp Apps That Can Simplify Your Plain Text Life, And Work Alongside an Obsidian Vault</a><br>
</li>
<li><a href="https://ellanew.com/2023/08/17/setapp-saves-me-hundreds-a-year" class="wikilink">2023-08-17 How Setapp Saves Me Hundreds of Dollars Every Year</a><br>
</li>
<li><a href="https://ellanew.com/2026/03/23/ptpl-200-setapp-evaluation-part-1" class="wikilink">2026-03-23 <span class="small-caps">PTPL</span> 200 - Setapp saved me from myself, but now it’s time to re-evaluate</a><br>
</li>
<li><a href="https://ellanew.com/2026/04/06/ptpl-202-replacing-setapp" class="wikilink">2026-04-06 <span class="small-caps">PTPL</span> 202 - Replacing setapp - 7 down, 2 to go</a></li>
</ul>
<p>I have to admit this whole replacing-Setapp thing kind of snuck up on me. I had cancelled my subscription several months ago so as not to miss the deadline before another year’s fee was taken from my account, but didn’t seriously start putting alternatives in place until the old ones stopped working.</p>
<p>It’s time to live without renting an app catalog!</p>
<p>I’ll only be talking in any detail about the Setapp apps I used often. Those that doing without cause friction I’m not willing to live with. Replacements will be free or one-time purchases wherever possible. Prices are in <span class="small-caps">USD</span> and are current as of September 2026.</p>
<p>Here’s the full list of apps I had installed before my Setapp subscription expired. Apps in bold are those I’ve bought outright or replaced. The rest are those I wasn’t using at that time.</p>
<ul>
<li>Antinote<br>
</li>
<li><strong>CleanMyMac</strong><br>
</li>
